From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Erik Bourget <erik@ebourget.net>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 15:48:59 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] soc: apple: clpc: Let the T8132 GPU driver report its work

T8132's G16 firmware keeps GFX powered while the GPU idles, as T6040's
does for its whole lifetime, so the GFX power state says nothing about GPU
work. Let a T8132 GPU driver take the CLPC's host input, as on T6040 and
T8140: accept the T8132 CLPC as a provider, and allocate the input at
probe.

The T8132 floor still follows the GFX power state; a later change makes it
follow the reported work.

Signed-off-by: Erik Bourget <erik@ebourget.net>
(cherry picked from commit 3853550655d07071a1bc02d38830934672f9bf29)
Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
---
 drivers/soc/apple/clpc.c | 5 ++++-
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/soc/apple/clpc.c b/drivers/soc/apple/clpc.c
index b34a7bd14d..7b27085ca3 100644
--- a/drivers/soc/apple/clpc.c
+++ b/drivers/soc/apple/clpc.c
@@ -227,6 +227,7 @@ int apple_clpc_gpu_get(struct device *dev, struct apple_clpc_gpu **out)
 	if (!np)
 		return of_find_property(dev->of_node, "apple,clpc", NULL) ? -EINVAL : 0;
 	if (!of_device_is_compatible(np, "apple,t6041-clpc") &&
+	    !of_device_is_compatible(np, "apple,t8132-clpc") &&
 	    !of_device_is_compatible(np, "apple,t8140-clpc")) {
 		of_node_put(np);
 		return -EINVAL;
@@ -731,9 +732,11 @@ static int apple_clpc_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 	clpc->hw = of_device_get_match_data(dev);
 	/* T6040 firmware keeps GFX powered for its whole lifetime. A separate
 	 * host publication/idle input, not that supplier state, drives demand.
-	 * On T8140 the same input counts submissions for dense light work.
+	 * On T8140 the same input counts submissions for dense light work. The
+	 * T8132 GPU driver reports its work through it as well.
 	 */
 	if (of_device_is_compatible(dev->of_node, "apple,t6041-clpc") ||
+	    of_device_is_compatible(dev->of_node, "apple,t8132-clpc") ||
 	    clpc->hw->gpu_dense) {
 		clpc->gpu = kzalloc_obj(*clpc->gpu);
 		if (!clpc->gpu)
